<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Honda (1971) J. Theor. Biol. & Honda & Fisher (1978) Science 3D recursive dichotomous tree branching, effective leaf area optimization, and Leonardo da Vinci pipe-model cross-sectional area conservation — MorphoEval overall 52.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py` (weighted score: 53.6/100). The Pass 1 baseline implements only a 2D planar branching sketch at two angle pairs without Honda's (1971) full 3D local rotation-matrix recursion in the (v, v x z_hat) frame, omits the Honda & Fisher (1978) 2D (theta_1, theta_2) effective leaf area A_eff / A_total optimization landscape across 5-branch whorls, omits Leonardo da Vinci / Shinozaki pipe-model cross-sectional area conservation (d_0^2 = d_1^2 + d_2^2), omits the 4-archetype 3D crown morphospace and collinear theta_1 = theta_2 = 0 self-shaded ablation control, and does not segment or analyze the vendored Cornus controversa tiered crown specimen (`cornus_controversa_tiered_crown_specimen.jpg`). Overall 52.0/100 (faithfulness 49.0, reproducibility 58.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 55, Morphological realism / specimen match 42, Parameter expressivity 50, Morphometric validation 52, Source and data traceability 68, Code-to-model traceability 55, Reproducibility package 54. Output judged: docs/media/dichotomous_tree_branching_comparison.png: rendered output of 1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py at 8871db0, image/png, 79737 B, 1300×598 px, artifact_sha256 dad80c3426bb4219912d67817048ba6d8b2c74120493777eb856f243f74dff0d (sha256 dad80c3426bb4219912d67817048ba6d8b2c74120493777eb856f243f74dff0d), spec_fingerprint eda105b6a09bddde8549d14c48bd6a5e37008bf9238b3585daf3bc48336da26b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: eda105b6a09bddde8549d14c48bd6a5e37008bf9238b3585daf3bc48336da26b; artifact_sha256: dad80c3426bb4219912d67817048ba6d8b2c74120493777eb856f243f74dff0d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/cornus_controversa_tiered_crown_specimen.jpg=47cbd7225997789e..., datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/dichotomous_tree_branching_reference.json=9b8cd89b9fa19fbf...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Implement Honda's (1971) full 3D local rotation-matrix tree builder in the (v, v x z_hat) frame across 4 botanical crown archetypes (excurrent conifer, pagoda tiered Cornus/Terminalia, decurrent deliquescent hardwood, and weeping pendulous Salix) alongside Leonardo da Vinci / Shinozaki pipe-model diameter tapering (d_parent^2 = d_1^2 + d_2^2).",
        "remediation needed: Implement the Honda & Fisher (1978) Science 2D (theta_1, theta_2) effective leaf area optimization landscape A_eff(theta_1, theta_2) / A_total across 5-branch horizontal pagoda whorls, demonstrating the global optimum at Cornus controversa (26 deg, 56 deg) and Terminalia catappa (30 deg, 60 deg) versus the collinear theta_1 = theta_2 = 0 self-shaded ablation control.",
        "remediation needed: Segment and skeletonize the vendored Pagoda Dogwood (Cornus controversa 'Variegata') specimen (`cornus_controversa_tiered_crown_specimen.jpg`) to extract the 7 horizontal pagoda foliage tiers, woody branch skeleton, empirical bifurcation angles (theta_1, theta_2), and Leonardo area ratio (d_1^2 + d_2^2)/d_0^2, backed by runtime SHA-256 integrity checks and an 8-suite `--self-test`." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

